---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  serviceType: 'Managed AI operations and automation for small business',
  provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Vemor', url: 'https://vemor.ai' },
  description: 'Managed AI operations for small businesses: operations audit, system architecture, custom automation builds, and ongoing managed service. An alternative to hiring a fractional CTO.',
  areaServed: ['United States', 'Mexico'],
};
---
<Base
  title="Managed AI Operations for Small Business | Vemor"
  description="An operator who builds, not a consultant with a deck. Operations audits, custom AI automation, and ongoing managed service for small businesses. An alternative to a fractional CTO or IT hire."
  schema={schema}
  path="/operations"
>
  <section class="hero" style="min-height:0; padding-bottom:60px;">
    <span class="hero-tagline">Managed AI Operations</span>
    <h1>An operator who builds.<br /><span class="gold">Not a consultant with a deck.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      Most small businesses don't need a technology strategy. They need the invoice
      chased, the books reconciled, the phones answered, and the report on the desk
      Monday morning. That's what this service delivers: finished outcomes, run for you.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a href="https://Vemor.as.me/" class="btn-primary">Book a Discovery Call</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROCESS -->
  <div class="section-full soft">
    <div class="inner">
      <span class="label">What You're Buying</span>
      <h2 class="title">Audit. Architect. Build. Operate. Expand.</h2>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">1</div>
          <h3>Audit</h3>
          <p>We sit down and map your operation: where the hours go, where the errors hide, what a fix is actually worth. You get a written plan whether or not we go further.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">2</div>
          <h3>Architect</h3>
          <p>The system gets designed around your existing tools: your POS, your calendar, your spreadsheets. What to build, what to buy, what to leave alone.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">3</div>
          <h3>Build</h3>
          <p>Custom automation, AI agents, databases, integrations, even hardware like RFID tracking. Built by me, tested on your real work before it goes live.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">4</div>
          <h3>Operate</h3>
          <p>I monitor it, maintain it, and send you reports that prove it's working. When something breaks at 6 AM, that's my problem, not yours.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">5</div>
          <h3>Expand</h3>
          <p>Every report shows what else could be automated. When you're ready, we take the next task off your plate. Never before.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- WHAT KIND OF WORK -->
  <section>
    <span class="label">The Kind of Work This Covers</span>
    <h2 class="title">If it repeats, it can probably die.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Real examples from systems Vemor has built and runs today:</p>
    <div class="cards-3">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Daily reconciliation</h3>
        <p>Automated nightly reconciliation across a four-station operation, reading straight from the existing point-of-sale database. Payment errors and unauthorized discounts flagged same day instead of surfacing weeks later in accounting.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Physical asset tracking</h3>
        <p>RFID tracking for rental equipment across four locations, with automatic evening alerts when a unit is missing and not on an invoice. Hardware, software, and text alerts, built as one system.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Document intelligence</h3>
        <p>An automated research engine for a law practice that reads hundreds of legal filings, extracts and verifies the numbers with evidence for every figure, and produces a benchmark report in seconds instead of hours.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PRICING + FIT -->
  <div class="section-full soft">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="story-grid">
        <div class="story-content">
          <h4>What it costs</h4>
          <p>
            Engagements start at <strong style="color:var(--text);">$2,000/month</strong>, scoped to
            the work. That's less than a part-time hire, and it covers architecture,
            the build, and the ongoing operation. Not advice. Not a license fee.
            A running system with a human accountable for it. Some businesses shop
            for this under "fractional CTO." I don't use the title. I'm the operator
            who builds and runs the systems a CTO would only plan.
          </p>
          <h4>Not sure yet?</h4>
          <p>
            Start with a paid operations audit. A few days inside your workflow, then a
            written report: what to automate, what it costs, what it saves. If we go
            forward, the audit rolls into the engagement. If not, you keep the roadmap.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="story-content">
          <h4>Good fit</h4>
          <p>
            Owner-operated businesses drowning in repeatable work: auto services, clinics,
            legal practices, property and field services. Teams where the owner is still
            the one doing the reconciliation at 9 PM. English or Spanish speaking, or both.
          </p>
          <h4>Bad fit</h4>
          <p>
            Anyone shopping for a magic AI button, a one-time script with no owner, or the
            cheapest possible vendor. This is a working relationship. I take on a small
            number of clients and stay accountable to every one of them.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section style="text-align:center;">
    <h2 class="title">Tell me what's eating your week.</h2>
    <p class="sub" style="margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto;">
      First call is twenty minutes and costs nothing. I'll tell you straight whether
      automation is worth it for your case. Sometimes the honest answer is no.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-ctas" style="justify-content:center;">
      <a href="https://Vemor.as.me/" class="btn-primary">Book a Discovery Call</a>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-secondary">Send a Message</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
